WEBVTT

1
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.920 
"NATIVES"

2
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:26.840 
ALGERIA - 1943

3
00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.160 
We must rid France
of the German occupation

4
00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.440 
Come along! Come with me!

5
00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.880 
We must wash the French flag
with our blood!

6
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.280 
Come with me, men!

7
00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.400 
We must liberate France
and sort out this situation!

8
00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.640 
Come, you men!

9
00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.960 
We must liberate France.

10
00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:08.320 
Saïd!

11
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.040 
Come back!

12
00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.640 
Be reasonable.

13
00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.000 
Come back inside.

14
00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:36.560 
- Your grandfather never came back.
- Don't worry about me, Mother.

15
00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:41.240 
I want to help France.
I can't stay here.

16
00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.920 
I prefer the worst poverty
to losing you.

17
00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.800 
You have endured much worse.

18
00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.600 
Please, let me go.
It will be all right, Mother.

19
00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:02.920 
Pray for me.

20
00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.000 
Get in.

21
00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:11.880 
Move it!

22
00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.760 
Long live France!

23
00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.680 
Climb in.

24
00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:04.760 
MOROCCO - 1943

25
00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.120 
To the left...
Left!

26
00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:29.520 
I know that you Aït Tserouchen,
the mountain men.

27
00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.360 
are the French army's best fighters,

28
00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:35.120 
better than the other Berbers.

29
00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:36.680 
And you'll prove it!

30
00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.200 
Listen carefully now.

31
00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:42.160 
We permit raids in enemy territory
for food.

32
00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:45.440 
But hands off the women
or you'll be shot.

33
00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:48.520 
In France. No raids at all.

34
00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:50.000 
We show discipline!

35
00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:52.320 
It's our home, our motherland!

36
00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:57.960 
To the left...
Left!

37
00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:04.160 
Yassir, they make us march like mules.
Let's go back home.

38
00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:07.680 
Serve France with pride,
and France will be of service to you.

39
00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.040 
Why did you get us enlisted?

40
00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:14.240 
For the money...
so you can be married.

41
00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:15.320 
Forward...

42
00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:16.640 
March!

43
00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.680 
The Sergeant communicates
with his men...

44
00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.920 
SةTIF, ALGERIA - 1943

45
00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:30.160 
through verbal orders...

46
00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.000 
and through signals...

47
00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.800 
through verbal orders
and through signals...

48
00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.120 
used simultaneously.

49
00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:49.560 
<i>We're the men of Africa.
Come here from afar</i>

50
00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:53.080 
<i>We've come from the colonies
To save the fatherland</i>

51
00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:56.320 
<i>We've left behind
Our families and homes</i>

52
00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:00.200 
<i>And our hearts are full
Of invincible fervour</i>

53
00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.880 
<i>For we wish to bear high and proud</i>

54
00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.240 
<i>The cherished flag of sweet France</i>

55
00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:10.960 
<i>Should someone try to part us</i>

56
00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:14.320 
<i>We're here to die at her feet</i>

57
00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:18.160 
<i>Drums roll to mark our love
For our country and land</i>

58
00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:21.160 
<i>We've come from afar to die
We're the men of Africa</i>

59
00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:22.800 
At ease!

60
00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:34.000 
Company...

61
00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:35.800 
Halt!

62
00:08:36.920 --> 00:08:38.040 
Left turn!

63
00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:49.800 
Don't salute me here.

64
00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:53.120 
They always pick officers as targets.

65
00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:59.960 
Corporal Abdelkader, 2nd Company,
7th Algerian Infantry Regiment,

66
00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:01.200 
reporting. Sir!

67
00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:05.000 
What can your lads do?

68
00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:08.160 
No idea. Sir. They're my first group.

69
00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.360 
You got your rank how?

70
00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.520 
I passed the exam. Sir.

71
00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.960 
I took mine with the Boche.

72
00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:30.440 
Corporal Leroux reporting, sir.

73
00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.760 
You can go.

74
00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:00.840 
Praise be to God.

75
00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:04.160 
Take this German rifle.
The best.

76
00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:06.400 
You'll be the marksman.

77
00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:15.280 
Take it.

78
00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:22.120 
Hit the deck!

79
00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:54.600 
Don't blame him, Sergeant.

80
00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:56.760 
They're still green.

81
00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.760 
I have the power
of life and death over you!

82
00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:10.160 
Starting with you.

83
00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:12.680 
Yes...
Sergeant.

84
00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:29.640 
The Germans are dug in up there.
At ease.

85
00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:34.040 
Tomorrow, our mission
is to climb up to the Boche.

86
00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:35.720 
to flush them out.

87
00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:38.400 
We have to do it.

88
00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:40.280 
It's a light infantry job.

89
00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:43.920 
You'll lead the men.

90
00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:50.880 
Any trouble, take out a cigarette.

91
00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.760 
Before you light it,
it'll be over.

92
00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:54.720 
Yes, Sergeant.

93
00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:59.320 
- It reassures the lads behind.
- Yes, Sergeant.

94
00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:21.600 
Hitting a soldier isn't allowed.

95
00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:24.320 
I know the Sergeant from Tunisia.
He's a good man.

96
00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.880 
He knows his job.

97
00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:32.120 
Where are you from Saïd?

98
00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:36.200 
From total poverty.

99
00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:43.760 
Listen, in that uniform...
you are just like me.

100
00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:46.240 
You're like all of us.

101
00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:50.600 
We're the same family.
The army means equality.

102
00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:56.080 
Wait a while.
You'll get your share of bullets tomorrow.

103
00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:06.360 
Corporal...
Are you afraid?

104
00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:17.760 
Enough talk.

105
00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:20.560 
Tomorrow, you'll know...

106
00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:23.160 
if you're soldiers or not.

107
00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:40.160 
Your coffee, Sarge.

108
00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:43.920 
Thank you, Ali.

109
00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:45.720 
Careful. it's hot.

110
00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:55.960 
We'll be in for it tomorrow.

111
00:13:56.960 --> 00:14:00.400 
Yes, tomorrow we have a party.

112
00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:02.320 
God willing.

113
00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:27.040 
O Merciful Compassionate
Lord of the Worlds,

114
00:14:27.520 --> 00:14:30.120 
Merciful. Compassionate King
of Judgement Day.

115
00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:32.280 
You alone we worship
and seek help from.

116
00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:34.920 
Guide us along the right path...

117
00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:39.040 
Merciful. Compassionate King
of Judgement Day.

118
00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:45.160 
You alone we worship,

119
00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:48.000 
it is You whom we beseech,

120
00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:52.440 
Guide us along the right path...

121
00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.000 
God is great.

122
00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:45.200 
I declare that no God but Allah...

123
00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:48.680 
...and Mohammed is his Prophet.

124
00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:00.160 
Move forward!

125
00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:42.160 
Abdelkader, move!

126
00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:45.000 
Abdelkader!

127
00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:46.000 
Corporal!

128
00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:49.040 
What do we do?

129
00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:50.240 
Shut up!

130
00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:56.040 
Move!

131
00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.960 
We'll die if we stay here.

132
00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:16.400 
Messaoud!

133
00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:17.400 
Ahmed!

134
00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:18.400 
Saïd!

135
00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:19.760 
Let's go!

136
00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:53.680 
Colonel, the artillery!

137
00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:00.920 
Battery number 5.

138
00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:04.320 
938-991

139
00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:08.040 
Battery number 5.
Position 938-991.

140
00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:11.200 
- Copy.
- 903-940.

141
00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:14.280 
Battery number 4.
Position 903-940.

142
00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.120 
Bearing 1400, order 340.

143
00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:21.120 
Charge 5. Loaded.

144
00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:22.280 
First gun, ready!

145
00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:23.600 
Second gun, ready!

146
00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:24.520 
Attention... Fire!

147
00:18:34.520 --> 00:18:36.200 
Stay down! That's our side.

148
00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.920 
Larbi? Larbi!

149
00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:42.040 
Don't be afraid, my little friend...

150
00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.400 
we're not going to die today.

151
00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:07.600 
Forward, Messaoud, over there!

152
00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:11.320 
Move forward! Keep going!

153
00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:22.400 
Sergeant!

154
00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:23.760 
Stay behind me!

155
00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:33.760 
Ali, are you hurt?

156
00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:20.960 
Keep going!

157
00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:49.280 
Come out of there!

158
00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:00.560 
Open his mouth.

159
00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:07.080 
Stop!
What are you doing?!

160
00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:10.520 
We're soldiers, not savages.

161
00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:12.040 
Fuck you!

162
00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:12.880 
Scum!

163
00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:21.440 
We're pulling out!

164
00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:40.640 
Long live France!

165
00:24:03.240 --> 00:24:04.080 
Colonel...

166
00:24:05.440 --> 00:24:06.600 
How many casualties?

167
00:24:07.560 --> 00:24:08.520 
How many dead?

168
00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:11.360 
It's a magnificent victory.

169
00:24:12.360 --> 00:24:14.240 
For the first time
since the 1940 defeat...

170
00:24:14.240 --> 00:24:16.720 
our army has defeated the Germans.

171
00:24:17.960 --> 00:24:20.440 
France has regained glory
and the Allies' trust.

172
00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:21.680 
Write that.

173
00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:24.160 
A photo Colonel?

174
00:24:27.080 --> 00:24:28.360 
Write what I said.

175
00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:30.200 
Let's go.

176
00:26:00.160 --> 00:26:01.440 
Lower...

177
00:26:04.960 --> 00:26:06.560 
That's it!

178
00:26:10.880 --> 00:26:11.880 
Yes?

179
00:26:20.920 --> 00:26:21.800 
At ease.

180
00:26:22.360 --> 00:26:23.640 
What do you want?

181
00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:27.640 
I come to say thank you.

182
00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:31.000 
You save my life, Sergeant.

183
00:26:31.200 --> 00:26:32.600 
You want to thank me?

184
00:26:33.240 --> 00:26:35.680 
Make some coffee.
You can replace Ali.

185
00:26:36.400 --> 00:26:38.520 
If I'm pleased,
I'll promote you to First Class.

186
00:26:49.920 --> 00:26:51.440 
Well? What did he say?

187
00:26:52.160 --> 00:26:53.840 
Are we going home?

188
00:26:54.800 --> 00:26:56.600 
- Soon, God willing.
- Is it true?

189
00:26:57.160 --> 00:27:00.040 
Thank you, my friend.

190
00:27:00.280 --> 00:27:01.960 
Where's my chocolate?

191
00:27:03.760 --> 00:27:05.960 
- Here.
- Thank you.

192
00:27:17.800 --> 00:27:19.120 
No tomatoes for you.

193
00:27:21.880 --> 00:27:24.080 
- Why?
- They're not for you. Move!

194
00:27:27.080 --> 00:27:28.360 
What do you mean?

195
00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.280 
Let go of him!

196
00:27:37.160 --> 00:27:39.160 
You're cooking while he fights.

197
00:27:39.200 --> 00:27:40.280 
Yes, Sergeant.

198
00:27:42.720 --> 00:27:43.440 
Move it.

199
00:27:48.760 --> 00:27:51.200 
Why aren't the tomatoes for everyone?

200
00:27:51.480 --> 00:27:52.640 
He's right.

201
00:27:53.840 --> 00:27:55.480 
We want tomatoes too!

202
00:27:57.160 --> 00:27:58.160 
He's right!

203
00:28:00.200 --> 00:28:01.720 
Shut your mouths!

204
00:28:07.880 --> 00:28:09.040 
You're not happy?

205
00:28:37.000 --> 00:28:38.520 
No one will have any now...

206
00:28:39.320 --> 00:28:40.720 
Sergeant.

207
00:28:57.440 --> 00:29:01.240 
They're ready to die for us
but any injustice will cause mutiny.

208
00:29:01.760 --> 00:29:03.440 
You know the natives, Martinez...

209
00:29:03.840 --> 00:29:04.840 
Avoid that term, sir.

210
00:29:05.080 --> 00:29:06.760 
- The Muslims...
- That's just as bad.

211
00:29:07.120 --> 00:29:08.360 
So what do I call them?

212
00:29:08.560 --> 00:29:10.520 
The men, sir. The men.

213
00:29:26.200 --> 00:29:27.360 
What's going on here?

214
00:29:27.920 --> 00:29:28.640 
Captain,

215
00:29:29.240 --> 00:29:32.240 
we fight alongside
our French brothers in arms.

216
00:29:32.760 --> 00:29:36.000 
On the same terrain,
against the same enemy.

217
00:29:37.160 --> 00:29:38.960 
We must share the tomatoes too.

218
00:29:41.240 --> 00:29:43.600 
German bullets
don't pick and choose, sir.

219
00:29:49.120 --> 00:29:51.040 
Sergeant. When we have tomatoes

220
00:29:51.600 --> 00:29:53.400 
let everyone have them.

221
00:29:53.960 --> 00:29:54.960 
Yes, sir.

222
00:29:56.080 --> 00:29:57.280 
Thank you, sir.

223
00:30:06.360 --> 00:30:08.600 
<i>My boys... My dear boys!</i>

224
00:30:09.440 --> 00:30:12.280 
<i>The dream for which
so many have died</i>

225
00:30:13.000 --> 00:30:14.520 
is coming true at last!

226
00:30:15.960 --> 00:30:17.960 
Your wounds and suffering,

227
00:30:18.560 --> 00:30:19.680 
all the pain

228
00:30:19.960 --> 00:30:21.360 
<i>and bloodshed,</i>

229
00:30:21.640 --> 00:30:24.640 
<i>are the price to pay
to be on this journey</i>

230
00:30:24.640 --> 00:30:27.920 
<i>We shall soon see France again!
The motherland!</i>

231
00:30:28.840 --> 00:30:30.120 
We are going home!

232
00:31:16.360 --> 00:31:20.760 
PROVENCE - AUGUST 1944

233
00:32:15.120 --> 00:32:16.280 
Smell it.

234
00:32:19.080 --> 00:32:21.040 
- It's not like at home.
- No.

235
00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:22.640 
French soil, is better.

236
00:32:26.320 --> 00:32:27.960 
Look!

237
00:32:30.360 --> 00:32:33.720 
Long live France!

238
00:33:23.480 --> 00:33:24.800 
Do you speak French?

239
00:33:24.880 --> 00:33:26.320 
Yes, I understand it.

240
00:33:27.280 --> 00:33:29.360 
- What's your name?
- Messaoud.

241
00:33:31.400 --> 00:33:33.040 
And what's your name?

242
00:33:33.560 --> 00:33:34.600 
Irène.

243
00:33:44.440 --> 00:33:46.240 
The sergeant says,

244
00:33:46.480 --> 00:33:47.840 
"Go up the mountain."

245
00:33:48.040 --> 00:33:51.120 
I was scared
but I go up the mountain.

246
00:33:51.600 --> 00:33:53.840 
I go up the mountain,
I run and run.

247
00:33:54.040 --> 00:33:56.760 
Messaoud to my right,
Abdelkader to my left.

248
00:33:57.080 --> 00:33:59.040 
I'm not scared then.

249
00:34:00.960 --> 00:34:04.240 
But Germany shoots at us.
Left, right, everywhere it shoots.

250
00:34:04.600 --> 00:34:07.240 
Messaoud says,
"Lie down in the hole."

251
00:34:07.640 --> 00:34:10.240 
I don't speak.
The sergeant looks at me.

252
00:34:10.560 --> 00:34:11.960 
I look at the sergeant.

253
00:34:12.480 --> 00:34:14.080 
I know what he wants.

254
00:34:14.520 --> 00:34:17.920 
I take the grenade, pull the pin
and throw it at Germany.

255
00:34:20.120 --> 00:34:21.400 
All of Germany, they die.

256
00:34:28.440 --> 00:34:31.440 
I free a country, it's my country.

257
00:34:32.720 --> 00:34:34.800 
Even if I never saw it before.

258
00:34:35.920 --> 00:34:37.040 
It's my country.

259
00:34:37.680 --> 00:34:39.520 
Your country is all you like?

260
00:34:40.960 --> 00:34:44.280 
God willing, we'll beat Germany.
Thank you very much.

261
00:35:38.040 --> 00:35:38.720 
Look.

262
00:35:39.280 --> 00:35:41.320 
Iron Cross. German.

263
00:35:41.800 --> 00:35:42.920 
Very beautiful.

264
00:35:45.040 --> 00:35:46.440 
Dangerous soldier...

265
00:35:48.680 --> 00:35:49.720 
Take this.

266
00:35:52.400 --> 00:35:54.000 
Good quality.

267
00:35:55.560 --> 00:35:56.720 
Iron Cross.

268
00:36:55.280 --> 00:36:56.480 
<i>Unlucky</i>

269
00:36:58.760 --> 00:37:00.680 
Why unlucky?

270
00:37:02.720 --> 00:37:04.280 
I didn't know you.

271
00:37:08.000 --> 00:37:09.080 
Sorry.

272
00:37:09.200 --> 00:37:09.920 
Good night.

273
00:37:13.560 --> 00:37:14.880 
Why are you scared?

274
00:37:18.680 --> 00:37:20.720 
The Germans won't be back.

275
00:37:23.080 --> 00:37:24.400 
You wiped them out.

276
00:37:26.320 --> 00:37:27.640 
It's not that.

277
00:37:28.840 --> 00:37:29.920 
But...

278
00:37:32.120 --> 00:37:35.760 
In my country,
we don't go with French women.

279
00:38:50.560 --> 00:38:51.320 
Leave it!

280
00:38:52.920 --> 00:38:54.280 
Don't touch it!

281
00:38:54.600 --> 00:38:57.920 
It's a sin!
I swear in God's name.

282
00:38:58.240 --> 00:38:59.720 
Aren't you ashamed?

283
00:39:00.840 --> 00:39:02.880 
Why. Yassir?
Is it God's?

284
00:39:07.200 --> 00:39:09.840 
- Don't touch it.
- All right.

285
00:39:29.080 --> 00:39:30.200 
Look...

286
00:39:33.560 --> 00:39:35.960 
Their God suffered a lot.

287
00:39:36.880 --> 00:39:37.560 
A lot

288
00:39:41.960 --> 00:39:43.040 
Tell me, Yassir...

289
00:39:44.000 --> 00:39:45.560 
When I was little,

290
00:39:46.160 --> 00:39:48.760 
the French soldiers
killed our whole family.

291
00:39:51.080 --> 00:39:52.520 
Did they massacre them?

292
00:39:54.720 --> 00:39:56.320 
What did they call it?

293
00:39:57.600 --> 00:39:59.200 
They called it...

294
00:39:59.520 --> 00:40:00.760 
Pacification.

295
00:40:02.400 --> 00:40:03.440 
Pacification?

296
00:40:28.440 --> 00:40:32.400 
- Corporal, can you read?
- Yes.

297
00:40:35.600 --> 00:40:37.960 
I can't read.

298
00:40:39.720 --> 00:40:41.200 
I never went to school.

299
00:40:42.680 --> 00:40:46.360 
You can learn.
Listen, Saïd...

300
00:41:00.840 --> 00:41:03.000 
Corporal, come here!

301
00:41:13.320 --> 00:41:14.720 
It's a military handbook, Sergeant

302
00:41:15.600 --> 00:41:17.440 
"The Infantry NCO's Handbook"

303
00:41:18.200 --> 00:41:19.680 
You want to be a Colonel?

304
00:41:20.760 --> 00:41:23.040 
A Sergeant first, Sergeant.

305
00:41:26.360 --> 00:41:27.960 
Let me read you a passage.

306
00:41:30.480 --> 00:41:31.160 
"In theory,

307
00:41:31.840 --> 00:41:35.840 
"no soldier should return home
illiterate from the army.

308
00:41:37.560 --> 00:41:40.040 
"Classes are obligatory for all men

309
00:41:40.440 --> 00:41:42.200 
"upon their enlistment."

310
00:41:44.120 --> 00:41:48.040 
Yet none of these African troops
can read or write.

311
00:41:51.360 --> 00:41:52.160 
Saïd...

312
00:41:52.920 --> 00:41:54.720 
You want to learn to read?

313
00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:01.840 
It's too late, Sergeant.

314
00:42:04.120 --> 00:42:05.320 
And to read what?

315
00:42:19.080 --> 00:42:20.720 
Get me a clean shirt.

316
00:42:32.400 --> 00:42:33.640 
You'll come back?

317
00:42:34.760 --> 00:42:37.080 
Yes, I promise I come back

318
00:42:37.640 --> 00:42:38.560 
You wait for me?

319
00:42:39.400 --> 00:42:40.240 
Yes.

320
00:43:08.000 --> 00:43:12.840 
RHONE VALLEY - OCTOBER 1944

321
00:43:35.000 --> 00:43:37.160 
I never loved a girl like this.

322
00:43:38.320 --> 00:43:41.840 
I want to marry her,
have kids and make a family.

323
00:43:42.240 --> 00:43:43.880 
You sure work fast.

324
00:43:44.520 --> 00:43:46.640 
Marseilles is paradise.
Here, Corporal,

325
00:43:46.960 --> 00:43:49.320 
they respect me. I'm not a wog.

326
00:43:50.080 --> 00:43:52.400 
I swear!
I make my life in France.

327
00:43:52.520 --> 00:43:53.880 
You'll always be a wog.

328
00:43:54.200 --> 00:43:56.000 
Shut it!
Ever slept in sheets before?

329
00:43:56.560 --> 00:43:57.160 
Saïd!

330
00:43:58.000 --> 00:43:58.880 
Saïd! Get in!

331
00:44:01.120 --> 00:44:01.720 
Get in.

332
00:44:14.680 --> 00:44:16.000 
Aïcha!

333
00:44:50.360 --> 00:44:51.440 
Me and Mother 1903

334
00:45:04.640 --> 00:45:06.040 
What is this shit?

335
00:45:07.080 --> 00:45:09.040 
Only you French guys get leave?

336
00:45:09.160 --> 00:45:11.440 
- We've fought since Marseilles.
- Us, Italy.

337
00:45:11.680 --> 00:45:15.120 
We're off to Paris.
You need to get back to Wogland.

338
00:45:16.280 --> 00:45:18.480 
This wog says fuck you.

339
00:45:34.800 --> 00:45:37.040 
You miss home, your family?

340
00:45:42.080 --> 00:45:43.520 
Why speak Arabic?

341
00:45:48.120 --> 00:45:51.520 
Me too. I like to go leave
to see my mother.

342
00:45:59.120 --> 00:46:02.360 
- Any mail for me?
- There's none for you.

343
00:46:02.400 --> 00:46:04.720 
Look again. It's not normal.

344
00:46:04.960 --> 00:46:07.040 
I wrote three times.
Messaoud Souni.

345
00:46:07.040 --> 00:46:10.480 
- Or maybe I'm listed as dead.
- I said no.

346
00:46:10.520 --> 00:46:13.240 
- Private!
- There's nothing for you.

347
00:46:26.520 --> 00:46:28.200 
Here's Aïcha!

348
00:46:31.520 --> 00:46:32.800 
How is she?

349
00:46:33.760 --> 00:46:35.880 
Has Sergeant Martinez
rejected you?

350
00:46:36.080 --> 00:46:37.360 
Marrying a Moroccan?

351
00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:42.000 
Why are you hassling me?

352
00:46:42.680 --> 00:46:47.640 
Go to your Marseilles girl...
A Yank is probably fucking her now.

353
00:46:49.000 --> 00:46:51.560 
It doesn't matter.
Want to know why?

354
00:46:51.800 --> 00:46:54.880 
You're the one I want,
Aïcha

355
00:46:56.400 --> 00:46:58.400 
Our beautiful Aïcha.

356
00:46:59.920 --> 00:47:01.280 
She takes care of us.

357
00:47:04.760 --> 00:47:08.400 
- As God is my witness...
- Saïd calm down!

358
00:47:09.520 --> 00:47:11.840 
If you ever call me Aïcha again...

359
00:47:14.960 --> 00:47:16.120 
If any of you...

360
00:47:17.280 --> 00:47:18.920 
No problem, my brother.

361
00:47:20.600 --> 00:47:24.360 
- Everyone has understood.
- Stop it!

362
00:47:24.680 --> 00:47:25.960 
Leave him be. Calm down..

363
00:47:26.280 --> 00:47:29.800 
If anyone calls me Aïcha.
I'll kill him.

364
00:47:31.920 --> 00:47:32.680 
Let go of him.

365
00:47:32.800 --> 00:47:35.120 
- I'm not a child!
- Let go of him.

366
00:47:35.480 --> 00:47:37.640 
Let go of him!

367
00:47:38.840 --> 00:47:40.400 
You're mad!

368
00:47:42.960 --> 00:47:47.480 
Are you soldiers,
idiots, or what?!

369
00:47:48.240 --> 00:47:49.320 
Shame on you!

370
00:47:50.840 --> 00:47:52.360 
Get out of here!

371
00:47:53.840 --> 00:47:55.400 
Get out now!

372
00:47:56.320 --> 00:47:57.800 
Quickly!

373
00:47:59.320 --> 00:48:01.320 
And don't do that again!

374
00:48:01.800 --> 00:48:03.200 
Listen to me, you.

375
00:48:03.600 --> 00:48:05.200 
You're not a slave.

376
00:48:05.720 --> 00:48:07.440 
There are no slaves here!

377
00:48:08.160 --> 00:48:12.480 
No one here has bothered with me.
Except the Sergeant!

378
00:48:16.400 --> 00:48:20.360 
Learn your book by heart
to become a Colonel!

379
00:48:21.280 --> 00:48:22.840 
Who's becoming a Colonel?

380
00:48:23.040 --> 00:48:27.440 
This donkey? This mule?!

381
00:48:28.480 --> 00:48:31.080 
Why can't they become Colonels?

382
00:48:32.480 --> 00:48:36.600 
Why not him? And even him?

383
00:48:38.320 --> 00:48:40.040 
Why not!

384
00:48:44.040 --> 00:48:45.280 
So try...

385
00:48:49.160 --> 00:48:52.280 
It's over!
Get to your bunks!

386
00:48:52.480 --> 00:48:54.920 
Do it!

387
00:48:56.560 --> 00:48:58.760 
I want no more trouble!

388
00:49:05.920 --> 00:49:10.840 
THE VOSGES - NOVEMBER 1944

389
00:49:23.240 --> 00:49:24.640 
Yes, it looks ugly!

390
00:49:25.040 --> 00:49:26.600 
It'll be worse in there!

391
00:49:28.440 --> 00:49:29.840 
It'll be tougher than Italy.

392
00:49:30.800 --> 00:49:32.160 
But I have faith in you.

393
00:49:33.360 --> 00:49:36.760 
I have faith in you
to liberate the motherland.

394
00:49:39.280 --> 00:49:42.280 
The French people have placed
their fate in our hands.

395
00:49:42.560 --> 00:49:45.240 
and are watching us
with eyes full of hope.

396
00:49:47.760 --> 00:49:49.840 
We have to be up there by dark!

397
00:49:50.040 --> 00:49:53.160 
And, even dead, we shall be!
Even dead!

398
00:50:53.680 --> 00:50:54.840 
Is it Omar, Sergeant?

399
00:51:07.280 --> 00:51:08.000 
Sergeant...

400
00:51:08.640 --> 00:51:10.160 
I've taken the position.

401
00:51:13.160 --> 00:51:14.600 
I'm here, Sergeant.

402
00:51:18.000 --> 00:51:19.480 
I'm the boss around here!

403
00:51:19.560 --> 00:51:22.960 
I ordered you to regroup,
not to head off on your own!

404
00:51:23.560 --> 00:51:26.240 
I give the orders.
I got you all this far!

405
00:51:27.120 --> 00:51:28.680 
We've lost Omar!

406
00:51:35.760 --> 00:51:39.440 
Go to say we've taken the enemy position
and request orders.

407
00:51:40.520 --> 00:51:41.560 
Yes, Sergeant.

408
00:52:12.240 --> 00:52:13.240 
Sergeant?

409
00:52:16.160 --> 00:52:17.760 
I have news for you Saïd.

410
00:52:18.520 --> 00:52:19.880 
You're promoted Private First Class.

411
00:52:20.320 --> 00:52:21.440 
You're transferred to HQ.

412
00:52:21.960 --> 00:52:23.360 
Take your pack and go there.

413
00:52:25.480 --> 00:52:27.920 
I don't want to be First Class, Sarge.

414
00:52:29.760 --> 00:52:32.440 
I'm fine like I am now.

415
00:52:34.200 --> 00:52:35.200 
I was kidding!

416
00:52:51.040 --> 00:52:52.840 
Learn to fend for yourself.

417
00:52:53.840 --> 00:52:55.400 
I might die one day.

418
00:52:59.360 --> 00:53:01.360 
You're not going to die, Sarge.

419
00:53:02.000 --> 00:53:03.840 
You not say that, ever.

420
00:53:06.760 --> 00:53:08.920 
You're going to be alive

421
00:53:08.920 --> 00:53:11.400 
to become Captain, God willing.

422
00:53:13.400 --> 00:53:15.080 
Captain is too much paperwork.

423
00:53:32.800 --> 00:53:35.040 
Are French girls all like this?

424
00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:39.440 
She says she's with you for life
and then forgets you.

425
00:53:39.680 --> 00:53:41.200 
Is that how it is here?

426
00:53:42.120 --> 00:53:44.840 
When you get promoted,
pick a rich, pretty one.

427
00:53:46.360 --> 00:53:47.880 
She is beautiful...

428
00:53:51.440 --> 00:53:52.920 
Look at the photo

429
00:53:53.280 --> 00:53:56.040 
and tell me what you think.
The truth.

430
00:53:56.320 --> 00:53:58.280 
Is she serious or not serious?

431
00:53:58.720 --> 00:54:00.720 
- What is her name?
- Irène.

432
00:54:01.000 --> 00:54:02.480 
Irène's a pretty name.

433
00:54:05.600 --> 00:54:09.200 
We have to see this war through.
We'll return with honour.

434
00:54:09.800 --> 00:54:11.440 
Irène will be proud of you.

435
00:54:28.920 --> 00:54:29.960 
Listen to this.

436
00:54:30.520 --> 00:54:33.200 
"After the war,
I return to Marseilles, Irène.

437
00:54:33.200 --> 00:54:35.640 
"I send you kisses. I think of you...

438
00:54:35.760 --> 00:54:37.760 
"...day and night, Messaoud."

439
00:54:38.560 --> 00:54:40.400 
- Pretty, huh?
- It's like a song.

440
00:54:41.800 --> 00:54:42.920 
CENSORED

441
00:54:48.360 --> 00:54:49.680 
They're not idiots, Captain.

442
00:54:50.480 --> 00:54:53.800 
They've been away from home 20 months,
they're freezing here...

443
00:54:53.920 --> 00:54:54.920 
I know, Sergeant!

444
00:54:55.240 --> 00:54:57.240 
- The French get leave.
- No ships!

445
00:54:57.880 --> 00:54:59.680 
There were ships to bring them here,

446
00:54:59.960 --> 00:55:01.720 
but none to send them on leave?

447
00:55:03.760 --> 00:55:05.800 
We'd like to see our families,

448
00:55:06.000 --> 00:55:08.440 
like the mainland French.
It's unfair.

449
00:55:10.120 --> 00:55:13.920 
And the French get promotion
before anyone from North Africa!

450
00:55:14.160 --> 00:55:17.520 
You're doing good work.
I'll put you up for promotion.

451
00:55:18.120 --> 00:55:21.440 
I don't want it.
My men deserve it as much as me.

452
00:55:22.280 --> 00:55:24.040 
Corporal Abdelkader, for instance.

453
00:55:44.920 --> 00:55:46.080 
Don't sleep.

454
00:55:46.200 --> 00:55:47.560 
Wake up! Get up!

455
00:56:29.960 --> 00:56:31.280 
God rest his soul.

456
00:57:15.920 --> 00:57:17.120 
What is it?

457
00:57:17.840 --> 00:57:19.400 
What does it say?

458
00:57:19.880 --> 00:57:21.200 
Read it.

459
00:57:24.240 --> 00:57:25.600 
"Muslim soldier,

460
00:57:26.440 --> 00:57:30.200 
"know that you can cross
to the German side

461
00:57:30.560 --> 00:57:32.960 
"where you will be warmly welcomed

462
00:57:33.000 --> 00:57:34.920 
"and your life saved.

463
00:57:36.040 --> 00:57:39.560 
"Your leaders send you to die
in place of the French.

464
00:57:42.480 --> 00:57:44.880 
"Muslim soldier,

465
00:57:44.920 --> 00:57:46.760 
"you weren't born into slavery.

466
00:57:47.880 --> 00:57:50.160 
"Germany will give you
your freedom.

467
00:57:53.320 --> 00:57:56.080 
"The day of independence
has come for Africa."

468
00:57:58.120 --> 00:58:01.720 
What would you do without us,
Abdelkader?

469
00:58:04.960 --> 00:58:06.720 
You have something in mind?

470
00:58:08.360 --> 00:58:09.600 
Out with it,

471
00:58:09.840 --> 00:58:10.880 
man to man.

472
00:58:12.920 --> 00:58:15.640 
De Gaulle said
we're fighting for liberty.

473
00:58:16.520 --> 00:58:20.360 
I'm fighting with France
against Nazism.

474
00:58:56.400 --> 00:58:58.120 
Come out of your holes!

475
00:58:58.360 --> 00:58:59.800 
We have leave!

476
00:59:02.320 --> 00:59:03.080 
Come out!

477
00:59:03.560 --> 00:59:06.600 
There is leave! We're going home!

478
00:59:07.720 --> 00:59:10.600 
It is finished. It is finished.

479
00:59:38.640 --> 00:59:40.640 
These aren't to go home in.

480
00:59:48.240 --> 00:59:50.640 
This evening, there will be dancers!

481
01:00:06.720 --> 01:00:08.480 
She hasn't replied to my letters.

482
01:00:10.240 --> 01:00:11.640 
Be patient, soldier.

483
01:00:11.880 --> 01:00:14.520 
There's a war on.
The mail hasn't arrived.

484
01:00:14.520 --> 01:00:17.360 
It has.
There was none for me.

485
01:00:19.040 --> 01:00:20.240 
Leroux! Martinez!

486
01:00:23.320 --> 01:00:27.160 
Martinez, you're promoted to
Staff Sergeant. Congratulations!

487
01:00:27.360 --> 01:00:28.360 
Thank you, Captain.

488
01:00:28.600 --> 01:00:31.640 
And you are Sergeant now, Leroux.
Congratulations.

489
01:00:33.320 --> 01:00:34.560 
Try to find stripes.

490
01:00:36.840 --> 01:00:37.960 
Well done, Leroux.

491
01:00:38.240 --> 01:00:39.600 
Thank you, Staff Sergeant.

492
01:00:46.760 --> 01:00:47.680 
Messaoud!

493
01:00:49.080 --> 01:00:51.760 
The girls will go wild for you
in those boots!

494
01:00:56.600 --> 01:00:58.520 
Do you like your coat, Corporal?

495
01:00:59.040 --> 01:01:00.280 
Yes, I suppose.

496
01:01:09.200 --> 01:01:10.320 
God keep you.

497
01:01:12.120 --> 01:01:12.880 
Amen.

498
01:01:41.800 --> 01:01:42.600 
Saïd!

499
01:01:45.400 --> 01:01:47.640 
He wears me out!
I have to go.

500
01:01:51.520 --> 01:01:52.720 
Here I am!

501
01:01:53.040 --> 01:01:53.840 
Sit yourself down.

502
01:02:01.520 --> 01:02:02.280 
Whisky.

503
01:02:03.280 --> 01:02:04.680 
Like in America.

504
01:02:13.480 --> 01:02:15.560 
Excuse me, Sarge, it burns!

505
01:02:19.200 --> 01:02:20.240 
Just a second...

506
01:02:34.720 --> 01:02:35.960 
Have a cigar.

507
01:02:37.440 --> 01:02:39.800 
- Is it for me?
- Of course it's for you.

508
01:02:42.320 --> 01:02:43.600 
You know,

509
01:02:44.200 --> 01:02:46.840 
I don't usually smoke cigars,

510
01:02:47.440 --> 01:02:48.480 
but I will now.

511
01:02:53.400 --> 01:02:55.080 
I like you, Saïd.

512
01:02:57.520 --> 01:02:59.000 
Me too, Sarge.

513
01:03:00.280 --> 01:03:01.440 
I like you too.

514
01:03:02.160 --> 01:03:03.600 
You deserve to be First Class.

515
01:03:05.720 --> 01:03:08.040 
The whole unit does.
But Staff can't see that.

516
01:03:09.320 --> 01:03:12.120 
They can't tell, they don't know us.

517
01:03:16.720 --> 01:03:19.760 
We'll liberate the country
and go home.

518
01:03:27.160 --> 01:03:28.320 
But, Sarge...

519
01:03:28.720 --> 01:03:32.800 
Here too is our home.

520
01:03:34.000 --> 01:03:35.040 
It's France.

521
01:03:35.160 --> 01:03:38.160 
We're fighting for her,
for the motherland.

522
01:03:38.320 --> 01:03:41.080 
Here is our home and I know

523
01:03:41.920 --> 01:03:43.800 
you're like us too...

524
01:03:46.920 --> 01:03:48.000 
An Arab.

525
01:03:50.520 --> 01:03:51.960 
What did you just say?

526
01:03:53.400 --> 01:03:56.520 
I see photo of your mother
in the shirt.

527
01:03:59.600 --> 01:04:01.120 
It's incredible.

528
01:04:01.720 --> 01:04:04.920 
Put the photo of your mother

529
01:04:05.600 --> 01:04:08.720 
next to photo of my mother,
they look like sisters.

530
01:04:09.160 --> 01:04:11.040 
You searched my things,
you bastard!

531
01:04:15.480 --> 01:04:17.960 
Shit-stirring scum!

532
01:04:21.120 --> 01:04:24.720 
Never talk about this again
or I'll kill you.

533
01:04:26.200 --> 01:04:27.120 
Get lost!

534
01:05:02.480 --> 01:05:03.880 
Fall in! Attention!

535
01:05:17.080 --> 01:05:17.920 
At ease!

536
01:06:50.400 --> 01:06:51.880 
What is this shit?!

537
01:06:55.000 --> 01:06:55.960 
Sit down!

538
01:07:03.120 --> 01:07:06.400 
I'm taking my leave!

539
01:07:27.440 --> 01:07:30.160 
<i>With her potatoes
And mouldy beans</i>

540
01:07:30.640 --> 01:07:33.200 
<i>France is our mother
She feeds us</i>

541
01:07:33.520 --> 01:07:34.600 
Listen!

542
01:07:38.880 --> 01:07:41.280 
Listen to me, my brothers!

543
01:07:43.040 --> 01:07:46.840 
When I enlisted,
I listened to De Gaulle.

544
01:07:47.120 --> 01:07:50.400 
He said France was fighting
for freedom around the world.

545
01:07:50.680 --> 01:07:55.240 
I thought the war would give us
the rights of our French brothers.

546
01:07:56.440 --> 01:07:58.600 
We're all fighting against Hitler.

547
01:07:59.040 --> 01:08:02.040 
for liberty,
equality and fraternity.

548
01:08:04.600 --> 01:08:07.480 
It's about time they gave us
some of that liberty,

549
01:08:07.600 --> 01:08:10.800 
that equality
and, above all, that fraternity!

550
01:08:25.800 --> 01:08:28.600 
We're changing
the destiny of France!

551
01:08:30.320 --> 01:08:32.320 
Things must change for us too!

552
01:08:32.600 --> 01:08:33.920 
Stand aside!

553
01:08:36.040 --> 01:08:37.240 
You're asking for it!

554
01:08:37.520 --> 01:08:39.760 
You keep stirring up shit!

555
01:08:40.040 --> 01:08:41.680 
The French reward themselves,

556
01:08:41.720 --> 01:08:43.720 
then you white Africans,

557
01:08:43.960 --> 01:08:45.920 
and we Natives are forgotten.

558
01:08:46.480 --> 01:08:47.520 
There are quotas.

559
01:08:50.000 --> 01:08:51.040 
Quotas?

560
01:08:53.040 --> 01:08:54.480 
Why didn't you tell us?

561
01:08:55.480 --> 01:08:58.640 
You can't understand,
so shut up and step down!

562
01:08:59.000 --> 01:09:03.160 
Why can't I understand?
A wog has less of a brain than you?

563
01:09:03.560 --> 01:09:06.160 
Wogs aren't capable of leadership.

564
01:09:09.840 --> 01:09:11.520 
That day will come, Sergeant.

565
01:09:12.520 --> 01:09:15.040 
Pardon me...
"Staff" Sergeant.

566
01:09:42.800 --> 01:09:44.120 
What are you doing here?

567
01:09:46.000 --> 01:09:48.080 
I tried to get to Marseilles.

568
01:09:49.480 --> 01:09:52.800 
The French get leave,
we get nothing. Is that normal?

569
01:09:53.480 --> 01:09:54.480 
Is it normal?

570
01:09:55.600 --> 01:09:56.760 
You tried to desert.

571
01:09:58.080 --> 01:09:59.000 
Are you crazy?

572
01:10:00.520 --> 01:10:01.800 
I have to see her.

573
01:10:06.640 --> 01:10:08.440 
Why are you here, Corporal?

574
01:10:11.960 --> 01:10:16.080 
I had a fight with Martinez,
the Staff Sergeant.

575
01:10:20.480 --> 01:10:22.080 
Got a Gauloise?

576
01:10:29.200 --> 01:10:33.080 
They're at the front.
Their position is secret.

577
01:10:33.600 --> 01:10:34.600 
Write to him.

578
01:10:36.120 --> 01:10:39.760 
I already have, several times.
There's been no reply.

579
01:10:46.520 --> 01:10:47.520 
Tell me...

580
01:10:49.480 --> 01:10:50.800 
Is he dead?

581
01:10:52.520 --> 01:10:54.400 
Give me his name. We'll find out.

582
01:10:55.960 --> 01:10:58.400 
Messaoud Souni.

583
01:10:59.800 --> 01:11:02.720 
He's with the 7th
Algerian Infantry.

584
01:11:05.920 --> 01:11:08.520 
If we hear anything,
we'll let you know.

585
01:11:10.800 --> 01:11:12.120 
Thank you.

586
01:11:12.840 --> 01:11:15.680 
Colonel, we must be firm
with the Muslims.

587
01:11:16.200 --> 01:11:18.680 
Punish this Corporal as a warning.

588
01:11:19.160 --> 01:11:21.760 
Rambert, tell me something...

589
01:11:22.640 --> 01:11:23.720 
Yes, Colonel?

590
01:11:23.880 --> 01:11:26.840 
Before joining De Gaulle
at the last minute,

591
01:11:27.240 --> 01:11:28.880 
what were you in Vichy?

592
01:11:35.080 --> 01:11:36.960 
- Martinez.
- Yes, sir.

593
01:11:37.040 --> 01:11:40.120 
You know the Muslims.
What do we do with him?

594
01:11:40.680 --> 01:11:42.800 
He's loyal to France, Colonel.

595
01:11:43.280 --> 01:11:44.560 
All my men are patriots.

596
01:11:50.200 --> 01:11:52.600 
Corporal, you risk
a court-martial!

597
01:11:53.160 --> 01:11:55.040 
- There is injustice, Colonel.
- Silence!

598
01:11:55.760 --> 01:11:59.400 
We must strive together
towards one goal: our victory.

599
01:11:59.760 --> 01:12:01.920 
France needs us, all of us.

600
01:12:02.320 --> 01:12:04.560 
Do you understand what I'm saying?

601
01:12:06.360 --> 01:12:07.240 
Yes, Colonel.

602
01:12:12.720 --> 01:12:15.600 
In Alsace, the 35th US Division

603
01:12:15.920 --> 01:12:17.000 
has broken through.

604
01:12:17.320 --> 01:12:21.560 
They're under attack and require
reinforcements and ammunition.

605
01:12:22.560 --> 01:12:24.920 
We must hold this bridgehead

606
01:12:25.560 --> 01:12:27.880 
until the offensive
a few days from now.

607
01:12:28.480 --> 01:12:31.320 
Captain Durieux needs brave men,

608
01:12:31.680 --> 01:12:32.720 
men of experience.

609
01:12:33.240 --> 01:12:35.160 
It's a very dangerous mission.

610
01:12:38.680 --> 01:12:40.440 
I volunteer, Colonel.

611
01:12:42.280 --> 01:12:45.640 
Corporal,
I give you my word of honour,

612
01:12:45.920 --> 01:12:49.080 
that the rewards for yourself
and all the brave men

613
01:12:49.360 --> 01:12:51.200 
who contribute to
this historic exploit

614
01:12:51.560 --> 01:12:53.280 
will be worthy of the feat.

615
01:12:54.200 --> 01:12:56.640 
You will be the first
to reach Alsace.

616
01:12:57.280 --> 01:12:59.920 
All of France will watch
and remember you.

617
01:13:02.440 --> 01:13:04.960 
I shall fight with
my body and soul, Colonel,

618
01:13:05.520 --> 01:13:07.200 
as I have always done.

619
01:13:11.080 --> 01:13:12.480 
Corporal Abdelkader.

620
01:13:12.880 --> 01:13:14.640 
He's a man of his word.

621
01:13:15.160 --> 01:13:18.800 
There's no time to lose.
Get your unit's ammunition.

622
01:13:19.960 --> 01:13:21.160 
Captain...

623
01:13:23.400 --> 01:13:25.360 
Private Messaoud is in jail.

624
01:13:26.240 --> 01:13:28.480 
We need our marksman.
I'll see to it.

625
01:13:28.680 --> 01:13:29.680 
Thank you, Captain.

626
01:13:46.680 --> 01:13:48.160 
Tell the men to keep quiet.

627
01:13:48.920 --> 01:13:51.160 
Quiet!
We're nearing the German lines.

628
01:13:51.320 --> 01:13:53.320 
Keep quiet and control the mules.

629
01:15:06.600 --> 01:15:07.880 
Larbi?!

630
01:15:48.800 --> 01:15:49.800 
Why?

631
01:15:50.240 --> 01:15:53.080 
Why? My God? Why?!

632
01:16:29.000 --> 01:16:31.080 
The Captain and Leroux are dead.

633
01:16:33.040 --> 01:16:34.640 
We've lost five men too.

634
01:16:37.360 --> 01:16:39.440 
You're in charge now.

635
01:16:44.280 --> 01:16:45.720 
It is your decision.

636
01:16:48.680 --> 01:16:51.760 
Either you help the Americans
hold the line...

637
01:16:55.200 --> 01:16:57.200 
or you turn back.

638
01:17:10.280 --> 01:17:12.400 
Fetch the mule,
we're going on!

639
01:17:12.720 --> 01:17:14.720 
We've lost the ammunition!

640
01:17:14.760 --> 01:17:16.840 
- He's right.
- Silence!

641
01:17:17.240 --> 01:17:19.200 
We'll be the first French troops
in Alsace.

642
01:17:19.800 --> 01:17:21.720 
If we manage to hold...

643
01:17:21.840 --> 01:17:24.160 
the American positions, believe me...

644
01:17:26.000 --> 01:17:27.520 
we'll get what we deserve.

645
01:17:28.520 --> 01:17:29.320 
You'll get nothing!

646
01:17:30.120 --> 01:17:31.840 
Haven't you realised yet?

647
01:17:32.840 --> 01:17:34.600 
I've just given
my brother for France.

648
01:17:35.800 --> 01:17:36.600 
Enough!

649
01:17:36.920 --> 01:17:38.160 
Enough!

650
01:17:40.640 --> 01:17:42.240 
Corporal, be reasonable!

651
01:17:43.840 --> 01:17:44.960 
Be reasonable!

652
01:17:45.200 --> 01:17:46.800 
You want to kill each other?!

653
01:17:47.000 --> 01:17:48.440 
Enough have died already!

654
01:17:49.160 --> 01:17:51.000 
Corporal, pull yourself together!

655
01:17:51.320 --> 01:17:53.320 
Our comrades are dead!

656
01:17:54.600 --> 01:17:56.520 
Thanks to God, we are alive!

657
01:17:58.280 --> 01:18:01.440 
Corporal, God bless your family.

658
01:18:02.720 --> 01:18:03.840 
He's right.

659
01:18:05.360 --> 01:18:08.160 
- There's no point any more.
- What's wrong with you?

660
01:18:09.080 --> 01:18:11.160 
You want to be a Sergeant?
Too late!

661
01:18:12.240 --> 01:18:14.360 
You don't understand anything!

662
01:18:15.160 --> 01:18:18.040 
We're doing our duty
be going to Alsace!

663
01:18:20.640 --> 01:18:23.200 
Even if we pay 10 or
100 times this price.

664
01:18:23.480 --> 01:18:24.880 
We shall pay!

665
01:18:27.360 --> 01:18:29.400 
And they'll know us for it.

666
01:18:31.520 --> 01:18:33.160 
What's wrong with you?

667
01:18:35.080 --> 01:18:36.120 
Listen, Yassir...

668
01:18:37.760 --> 01:18:40.000 
You want to go home
with nothing?

669
01:18:41.040 --> 01:18:42.720 
We see it through to the end.

670
01:18:43.240 --> 01:18:46.360 
Your brother, God rest him,
won't have died for nothing.

671
01:18:51.160 --> 01:18:53.480 
Saïd, please go...

672
01:18:54.480 --> 01:18:56.080 
Bring back the mule.

673
01:18:56.680 --> 01:18:57.880 
Don't argue anymore.

674
01:18:58.400 --> 01:19:00.600 
It's over now. Go quickly.

675
01:19:26.560 --> 01:19:27.880 
Come here...

676
01:19:29.160 --> 01:19:30.800 
Come, my beautiful...

677
01:19:42.640 --> 01:19:43.440 
Come...

678
01:19:45.560 --> 01:19:47.920 
Don't make this difficult.

679
01:19:48.240 --> 01:19:50.080 
I'm tired...

680
01:19:51.520 --> 01:19:52.800 
Be good.

681
01:19:53.440 --> 01:19:55.280 
I can't run after you...

682
01:19:57.000 --> 01:19:58.520 
For the love of God!

683
01:22:18.040 --> 01:22:19.640 
Yassir, round the back!

684
01:23:51.400 --> 01:23:52.480 
The French!

685
01:23:57.360 --> 01:24:00.320 
You're alone?
Where are the others?

686
01:25:55.280 --> 01:25:57.800 
We'll defend the position, Staff Sergeant.

687
01:25:59.760 --> 01:26:02.160 
We'll hold it
until the Army arrives.

688
01:26:03.520 --> 01:26:05.560 
I would have done the same...

689
01:26:08.960 --> 01:26:10.080 
...Corporal.

690
01:26:17.640 --> 01:26:19.680 
I have to go see to the men.

691
01:26:33.320 --> 01:26:35.480 
I hope that you die.

692
01:26:40.440 --> 01:26:41.560 
Sergeant...

693
01:26:42.920 --> 01:26:44.320 
Staff Sergeant!

694
01:28:59.480 --> 01:29:01.400 
You'd never know
there was a war on..

695
01:29:05.800 --> 01:29:07.640 
What are we doing here?

696
01:29:11.800 --> 01:29:15.600 
After the war,
you will stay in the army,

697
01:29:16.200 --> 01:29:19.520 
You'll rise up the ranks and
become a Sergeant.

698
01:29:22.680 --> 01:29:24.680 
I don't want to be a Sergeant!

699
01:29:27.000 --> 01:29:29.360 
Some have the right to it,
others don't.

700
01:29:31.160 --> 01:29:33.120 
God forgets me for the moment.

701
01:29:38.400 --> 01:29:40.560 
Have you ever given
an order to anyone?

702
01:29:43.400 --> 01:29:44.840 
Never.

703
01:29:49.320 --> 01:29:50.920 
Tell me honestly

704
01:29:51.640 --> 01:29:53.480 
Will we survive this?

705
01:30:20.480 --> 01:30:21.920 
Listen, Saïd...

706
01:30:22.800 --> 01:30:24.480 
We've always survived...

707
01:30:25.200 --> 01:30:26.760 
together.

708
01:30:27.000 --> 01:30:28.840 
Did you forget that?

709
01:30:30.880 --> 01:30:32.880 
We are in God's hands.

710
01:30:51.160 --> 01:30:52.400 
Thank you, Madame.

711
01:30:59.960 --> 01:31:01.720 
Enjoy your meal, gentlemen.

712
01:31:02.240 --> 01:31:03.360 
Thank you, Madame.

713
01:31:07.000 --> 01:31:08.960 
Who can live in this cold?

714
01:31:11.120 --> 01:31:12.400 
The French!

715
01:32:02.440 --> 01:32:04.240 
Can I fetch milk
for the children?

716
01:32:25.680 --> 01:32:27.440 
Does she give a lot of milk?

717
01:32:29.960 --> 01:32:31.640 
Two or three buckets.

718
01:32:38.040 --> 01:32:38.960 
Want to try?

719
01:32:40.040 --> 01:32:40.880 
Sure...

720
01:33:09.920 --> 01:33:11.240 
You're never afraid?

721
01:33:13.960 --> 01:33:15.320 
Sometimes I am.

722
01:33:17.560 --> 01:33:19.560 
But tonight I'm not afraid.

723
01:40:21.760 --> 01:40:23.240 
Lord God...

724
01:40:24.040 --> 01:40:26.440 
I declare that there is
no God but Allah...

725
01:41:32.120 --> 01:41:35.520 
- I'll get Martinez.
- Wait, Saïd.

726
01:41:35.760 --> 01:41:37.640 
Listen to me...

727
01:41:37.960 --> 01:41:39.800 
Messaoud is dead.

728
01:41:41.720 --> 01:41:43.360 
Be careful, my brother.

729
01:41:44.320 --> 01:41:45.880 
Wait...

730
01:41:48.160 --> 01:41:49.080 
Yassir!

731
01:41:49.560 --> 01:41:50.760 
Cover us!

732
01:41:53.720 --> 01:41:55.160 
1, 2...

733
01:41:55.480 --> 01:41:56.160 
Go!

734
01:42:15.040 --> 01:42:16.880 
Sarge, get up!

735
01:42:26.720 --> 01:42:27.880 
Get up!

736
01:42:32.760 --> 01:42:33.640 
Come on!

737
01:43:09.840 --> 01:43:10.800 
Yassir!

738
01:43:11.600 --> 01:43:13.520 
Cover me, I'm coming!

739
01:43:27.840 --> 01:43:29.840 
Get out! Hurry!

740
01:43:36.280 --> 01:43:37.960 
Come on, let's go!

741
01:43:38.280 --> 01:43:39.560 
Move yourself!

742
01:44:03.520 --> 01:44:05.200 
Get up! Get up!

743
01:44:07.720 --> 01:44:10.120 
Get up for pity's sake!

744
01:45:08.720 --> 01:45:09.680 
Brothers...

745
01:45:10.160 --> 01:45:11.640 
I'm with you!

746
01:45:11.920 --> 01:45:13.080 
Don't shoot!

747
01:45:13.320 --> 01:45:14.320 
Okay.

748
01:47:23.160 --> 01:47:26.040 
Don't stop! Keep going!
Forward!

749
01:47:28.960 --> 01:47:29.960 
Colonel...

750
01:47:31.560 --> 01:47:32.520 
Colonel!

751
01:47:34.320 --> 01:47:36.280 
- Stop!
- Let me see the Colonel.

752
01:47:36.560 --> 01:47:37.960 
- What?
- Let me speak to him.

753
01:47:38.000 --> 01:47:40.560 
- See your Sergeant.
- He's dead. Captain too.

754
01:47:40.840 --> 01:47:42.000 
So where's your unit?

755
01:47:44.080 --> 01:47:46.600 
I don't have one.
They're all dead.

756
01:47:47.760 --> 01:47:48.520 
Sergeant!

757
01:47:49.880 --> 01:47:51.880 
You needed a Corporal?
Here's one.

758
01:47:51.920 --> 01:47:53.720 
Get your pack and follow us.

759
01:48:15.560 --> 01:48:16.800 
Look over here!

760
01:48:19.440 --> 01:48:22.000 
The French forces free Alsace.

761
01:48:25.280 --> 01:48:26.240 
This way!

762
01:48:26.680 --> 01:48:27.760 
Smile!

763
01:48:59.680 --> 01:49:03.320 
<i>60 years later</i>

764
01:53:21.200 --> 01:53:25.840 
<i>In 1959, a law was passed to freeze
the pensions of soldiers</i>

765
01:53:25.880 --> 01:53:29.760 
<i>from former French colonies
about to become independent.</i>

766
01:53:29.800 --> 01:53:32.200 
<i>In 2002, after endless hearings,</i>

767
01:53:32.320 --> 01:53:34.920 
<i>the French government was
ordered by Europe</i>

768
01:53:35.040 --> 01:53:37.240 
<i>to pay the pensions in full.</i>

769
01:53:37.360 --> 01:53:40.280 
<i>But successive governments</i>

770
01:53:40.360 --> 01:53:43.320 
<i>have refused to pay.</i>

771
01:53:48.040 --> 01:53:51.440 
English subtitles by heaver
for Fileheaven
